{{PAGENAME}} are an important part of [[Gray Zone Warfare]]. They play a big role in firefights and often determine the outcome. Choosing the right [[Weapons|weapon]], [[Ammunition|ammo]] and gear is one of the most important parts in winning gunfights.

==Flight ballistics==
Bullet flight is simulated realistically in [[Gray Zone Warfare]]. Bullets have speed, are affected by gravity and air friction and can penetrate or ricochet when hitting objects. The specific flight characteristics of a bullet are determined by the ammo type, and the chance of a bullet penetrating or ricocheting off of an object is determined by the material of the object and the type of bullet. Bullets lose both damage and penetration power as they lose speed from air friction over long distances.

==Armor and penetration==
===NIJ Protection Level===
[[Gray Zone Warfare]] uses the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_body_armor_performance_standards#NIJ_armor_standard_(United_States) American NIJ system], the Protection Level is related to how well the vest protects from bullet penetration. When inspecting a vest, the top left of the preview image, you can see where the vest has plates. The locations of these plates are important, these are where you are protected from penetration.
<br>
'''The folowing levels are sorted in order of effectiveness (Worst to Best)'''<br>
I, IIA, IIA+, IIIA, IIIA+, III, III+, III++

==Armor materials==
Armor durability does not change the performance of the armor. But the armor material does matter a lot.
